feature: SLICE

requirements:
  - id: SLICE-1
    title: Slice Status
    description: >
      The slice CLI reports the current state of slice work: the active
      slice, the running Harvest timer, and the ticket's status. It is the
      read-back every other slice command and the orchestrator rely on.
    status: active                 # kept for current Spool; derived from items once extensions land
    interface: src/ports.rs
    deciders:
      - Matty
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-10-27
    rationale: >
      The one-timer rule and idempotent commands both depend on knowing the
      current state before acting. A read-only status command is the safest
      first piece and doubles as the orchestrator's read-back check.
    superseded_by:
    out_of_scope:
      - History or reporting of past slices
      - Slack focus status
    acceptance_criteria:
      - id: SLICE-1-1
        title: Nothing Active
        status: active
        description: >
          Given no active slice and no running Harvest timer,
          when status is run,
          then it reports no active slice and no running timer and exits zero.

      - id: SLICE-1-2
        title: Active Slice
        status: active
        description: >
          Given an active slice for ticket T with a running timer for T,
          when status is run,
          then it reports ticket T, the slice id, the running timer,
          and the ticket's current status, and exits zero.

      - id: SLICE-1-3
        title: State Mismatch
        status: active
        description: >
          Given a running Harvest timer whose ticket differs from the active
          slice's ticket, or a running timer with no active slice whether
          or not its notes name a ticket,
          when status is run,
          then it reports the mismatch with both values and exits non-zero.

      - id: SLICE-1-4
        title: Source Unavailable
        status: active
        description: >
          Given Harvest or the ticket system cannot be reached,
          when status is run,
          then it names the source that failed and exits non-zero,
          and does not report that source's state as empty.

    invariants:
      - id: SLICE-1-I1
        title: Status Is Read-Only
        status: active
        description: >
          For every run of status, in every starting state, Harvest, the
          ticket system, and local slice state are unchanged afterward.

  - id: SLICE-2
    title: Slice Open
    description: >
      Running slice open with a ticket number starts work on that ticket:
      a Harvest timer, an in-progress ticket, a branch and worktree, and a
      slice manifest, all checked against status before anything changes.
    status: active                 # kept for current Spool; derived from items once extensions land
    interface: src/ports.rs
    deciders:
      - Matty
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-10-27
    rationale: >
      Opening a slice is the entry point for every unit of work and exercises
      both integrations that matter most: Harvest timers and ticket updates.
      Making it deterministic means housekeeping never depends on the
      orchestrator remembering to do it. Harvest is tracked per ticket per
      day: every slice of ticket T on a given day logs to T's one entry for
      that day, the most recently updated entry dated today whose notes name
      T. Slice ids are internal to slice and never appear in Harvest notes or
      on tickets.
    superseded_by:
    out_of_scope:
      - Pausing, resuming, or closing slices
      - Spec authoring and approval
      - Launching test or implementation agents
      - Choosing which ticket to work on
      - Slack focus status
    acceptance_criteria:
      - id: SLICE-2-1
        title: Clean Open
        status: draft
        description: >
          Given no active slice, no running Harvest timer, and no Harvest
          entry for T today,
          when slice open is run with a valid ticket number T,
          then a new Harvest entry for T is running, noted with T and the
          ticket's title only, ticket T is in progress, a branch and worktree exist for the slice,
          a slice manifest records T and the base commit,
          and the slice is active.

      - id: SLICE-2-2
        title: Stray Timer Running
        status: active
        description: >
          Given no active slice and a Harvest timer running for ticket U
          or for no ticket,
          when slice open is run with ticket T,
          then the running timer is stopped before the timer for T starts,
          and the open otherwise completes as in SLICE-2-1.

      - id: SLICE-2-3
        title: Another Slice Active
        status: active
        description: >
          Given an active slice for ticket U,
          when slice open is run with a different ticket T,
          then it fails, names the active slice for U,
          and changes nothing.

      - id: SLICE-2-4
        title: Same Slice Already Open
        status: active
        description: >
          Given an active slice for ticket T with its timer running,
          when slice open is run with ticket T,
          then it reports that the slice is already open, changes nothing,
          and exits zero.

      - id: SLICE-2-5
        title: Unknown Ticket
        status: active
        description: >
          Given a ticket number that does not exist in the ticket system,
          when slice open is run with it,
          then it fails with an error naming the ticket and changes nothing.

      - id: SLICE-2-6
        title: Partial Failure
        status: draft
        description: >
          Given a step of slice open fails after an earlier step succeeded,
          when slice open is run,
          then it undoes the earlier steps it performed in reverse order,
          including restarting any timer it stopped, deleting an entry only
          if this run created it, and stopping an existing entry it
          restarted, reports which step failed, and exits non-zero.

      - id: SLICE-2-8
        title: Ticket Already Tracked Today
        status: draft
        description: >
          Given no active slice, no running Harvest timer, and a stopped
          Harvest entry for T dated today,
          when slice open is run with T,
          then that entry is running again, no new entry is created,
          and the open otherwise completes as in SLICE-2-1.

      - id: SLICE-2-7
        title: Same Slice Timer Stopped
        status: draft
        description: >
          Given an active slice for ticket T and no running Harvest timer,
          when slice open is run with ticket T,
          then T's entry for today is running, restarted if it exists and
          started otherwise,
          the ticket, branch, worktree, and manifest are unchanged,
          it reports that the slice was already open and its timer
          restarted, and it exits zero.

    invariants:
      - id: SLICE-2-I1
        title: At Most One Running Timer
        status: active
        description: >
          For every starting state and every outcome of slice open,
          at most one Harvest timer is running afterward.

      - id: SLICE-2-I2
        title: Failed Open Leaves No Trace
        status: active
        description: >
          For every run of slice open that exits non-zero, no time entry it
          created still exists, every entry that existed before is still
          there and running or stopped as it was, no manifest exists for the
          slice, and the ticket's status is what it was before the run.

  - id: SLICE-3
    title: Slice Pause
    description: >
      Running slice pause stops the active slice's timer when you switch
      away, leaving the slice, its ticket, branch, worktree, and manifest
      as they are so it can be resumed later.
    status: draft
    interface: src/ports.rs
    deciders:
      - Matty
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-11-02
    rationale: >
      Pausing through slice rather than hv keeps the timer owned by the
      slice, so a later resume restarts the same entry and the one-timer
      rule holds. Pausing is the command run most often, so it must be
      idempotent and refuse rather than guess when state is inconsistent.
    superseded_by:
    out_of_scope:
      - Pausing automatically when a session ends
      - Slack focus status
    acceptance_criteria:
      - id: SLICE-3-1
        title: Pause Running Slice
        status: draft
        description: >
          Given an active slice whose timer is running,
          when slice pause is run,
          then the timer is stopped, the slice is still active, the ticket,
          branch, worktree, and manifest are unchanged, and it exits zero.

      - id: SLICE-3-2
        title: Already Paused
        status: draft
        description: >
          Given an active slice and no running Harvest timer,
          when slice pause is run,
          then it reports that the slice is already paused, changes nothing,
          and exits zero.

      - id: SLICE-3-3
        title: Nothing To Pause
        status: draft
        description: >
          Given no active slice,
          when slice pause is run,
          then it reports that no slice is active, changes nothing,
          and exits non-zero.

      - id: SLICE-3-4
        title: Pause Mismatch
        status: draft
        description: >
          Given an active slice and a running Harvest timer for a different
          ticket or for no ticket,
          when slice pause is run,
          then it reports the mismatch with both values, changes nothing,
          and exits non-zero.

    invariants:
      - id: SLICE-3-I1
        title: Pause Never Starts Or Deletes
        status: draft
        description: >
          For every starting state, slice pause starts no timer, deletes no
          time entry, and leaves the ticket, local slice state, and manifest
          unchanged.

  - id: SLICE-4
    title: Slice Resume
    description: >
      Running slice resume restarts the paused active slice's timer, without
      needing the ticket number.
    status: draft
    interface: src/ports.rs
    deciders:
      - Matty
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-11-02
    rationale: >
      SLICE-2-7 already resumes a paused slice when it is opened again by
      ticket number. Resume is the same operation addressed to whatever slice
      is active, which is what you want after a break without having to
      remember the ticket.
    superseded_by:
    out_of_scope:
      - Resuming a slice other than the active one
    acceptance_criteria:
      - id: SLICE-4-1
        title: Resume Paused Slice
        status: draft
        description: >
          Given an active slice and no running Harvest timer,
          when slice resume is run,
          then the slice ticket's entry for today is running, restarted if
          it exists and started otherwise, the ticket, branch, worktree, and
          manifest are unchanged, and it exits zero.

      - id: SLICE-4-2
        title: Already Running
        status: draft
        description: >
          Given an active slice whose timer is running,
          when slice resume is run,
          then it reports that the slice is already running, changes nothing,
          and exits zero.

      - id: SLICE-4-3
        title: Nothing To Resume
        status: draft
        description: >
          Given no active slice,
          when slice resume is run,
          then it reports that no slice is active, changes nothing,
          and exits non-zero.

      - id: SLICE-4-4
        title: Resume Mismatch
        status: draft
        description: >
          Given an active slice and a running Harvest timer for a different
          ticket or for no ticket,
          when slice resume is run,
          then it reports the mismatch with both values, changes nothing,
          and exits non-zero.

    invariants:
      - id: SLICE-4-I1
        title: Resume Keeps One Timer
        status: draft
        description: >
          For every starting state and every outcome of slice resume, at most
          one Harvest timer is running afterward, and no time entry is
          deleted.

  - id: SLICE-5
    title: Slice Close
    description: >
      Running slice close ends the active slice: its timer is stopped, the
      ticket moves to review (or done), the manifest is marked closed, and
      no slice is active afterward. The
      branch and worktree are left for review and merge.
    status: draft
    interface: src/ports.rs
    deciders:
      - Matty
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-11-02
    rationale: >
      Close is the last housekeeping step of the lifecycle. Merging stays
      a human action, so close only records that the work is ready and
      frees the one-active-slice slot. Close posts no comment: slice ids are
      internal, and there is nothing yet worth telling the ticket's readers
      that the status change does not. Every step can therefore be undone.
    superseded_by:
    out_of_scope:
      - Merging, pushing, or opening a merge request
      - Removing the branch or worktree
      - Logging decisions
      - Commenting on the ticket
      - Closing a slice that is not the active one
      - Slack focus status
    acceptance_criteria:
      - id: SLICE-5-1
        title: Close To Review
        status: draft
        description: >
          Given an active slice for ticket T,
          when slice close is run,
          then the slice's timer is not running, T is in its configured
          review status, the manifest's status is closed, no slice is active,
          the branch and worktree still exist, and it exits zero.

      - id: SLICE-5-2
        title: Close To Done
        status: draft
        description: >
          Given an active slice for ticket T,
          when slice close is run with --done,
          then it completes as in SLICE-5-1 except that T is in its
          configured done status.

      - id: SLICE-5-3
        title: Close Paused Slice
        status: draft
        description: >
          Given an active slice and no running Harvest timer,
          when slice close is run,
          then it completes as in SLICE-5-1 without starting or stopping
          any timer.

      - id: SLICE-5-4
        title: Nothing To Close
        status: draft
        description: >
          Given no active slice,
          when slice close is run,
          then it reports that no slice is active, changes nothing,
          and exits non-zero.

      - id: SLICE-5-5
        title: Close Mismatch
        status: draft
        description: >
          Given an active slice and a running Harvest timer for a different
          ticket or for no ticket,
          when slice close is run,
          then it reports the mismatch with both values, changes nothing,
          and exits non-zero.

      - id: SLICE-5-6
        title: Close Partial Failure
        status: draft
        description: >
          Given a step of slice close fails after an earlier step succeeded,
          when slice close is run,
          then it undoes the earlier steps it performed in reverse order,
          including restarting a timer it stopped, reports which step
          failed, and exits non-zero.

    invariants:
      - id: SLICE-5-I1
        title: Failed Close Leaves No Trace
        status: draft
        description: >
          For every run of slice close that exits non-zero, the slice is
          still active, its timer's running state, the ticket's status, and
          the manifest are what they were before the run.
